  "fields": {
    "title": "Webdesign",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Today, there are many terms to describe the design of digital interfaces, such as screen design, webdesign, user interface (UI) design, user experience (UX) design, interaction design or digital design. However, these are often incorrectly used synonymously and are therefore difficult to distinguish from each other. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "UI and UX are often regarded as separate disciplines, but in practice it is difficult to separate them. This is because the experience and user-friendliness of an interface are directly related to its design. In principle, screen design refers to the same thing as interface design, namely the graphic implementation of interfaces with the aid of a suitable layout. Strictly speaking, the function of the graphic user interface is not included here, but as in graphic design, the form can only be separated from the function with difficulty, or ideally should not be separated at all. Experience and interaction design are also two different terms for the same thing: the development of human-machine interfaces, which are as easily understood as possible. The field of usability includes a variety of aspects such as the psychology of perception, cognition, semantics, usability, ergonomics and quality of experience. However, such an interface does not necessarily have to be visual, but a purely voice-controlled interaction is also possible, for example. ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Although UI and UX can be considered subcategories of webdesign, websites are no longer the only digital interfaces that need to be conceived and designed. This is why UI, UX, screen design and interaction design today usually also include the design of apps and applications for a wide variety of end devices such as televisions, smartphones, smart home devices, wearables and many more. Here, interface design plays an important role as a key factor for the acceptance of increasingly complex products that are integrated into systems. The term digital design is also increasingly used today to refer to the development of digital content of all kinds.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Background",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "The term webdesign is rarely used today because it does not include the design of interfaces outside the browser. But the special thing about webdesign is that in the early years of the web it not only referred to the visual design and conception of websites, but also included the implementation through code. This is why we prefer to use the term webdesign on this website.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
